{#def agent_id, ws_name, current_account, accounts, is_leased_imbue_cloud=False, current_color="#0b292b", is_stale=False, has_account=False, palette={}, selected_group="general", panel_scroll=False #}
{#
  The "Machine settings" pane: the workspace's own settings, grouped behind a
  left nav (General / Account / Backup) the same way the share pane groups its
  targets. Shared verbatim between the docked options panel
  (pages.WorkspaceOptionsModal) and the full settings page
  (pages.WorkspaceSettings, the browser-mode fallback).

  Sharing is deliberately NOT a group here -- the Share machine tab next door
  owns it, and a per-service list in two places would drift.

  is_leased_imbue_cloud is True for workspaces running on a host leased from
  Imbue Cloud. Such hosts are permanently bound to the leasing account to avoid
  confusing "account mixing", so the account group shows the bound account with
  a disabled Unlink control and offers no linking controls.

  current_color is the stored workspace color hex (#rrggbb); it pre-fills the
  hex input and pre-selects the matching palette swatch (if any).
  is_stale disables the picker controls when the workspace's provider's last
  discovery poll errored -- writes against an unreachable host would not be
  observable until provider recovery.
  palette is the {name: hex} map of pickable swatches (10 entries).

  Interactivity: /_static/workspace_settings.js (color + account),
  /_static/workspace_backups.js (the backup group) and
  /_static/workspace_settings_page.js (rename + destroy). The group nav is
  driven by /_static/workspace_options.js, which both surfaces load.

  ``panel_scroll`` makes the right-hand panel the scroller (and pulls its
  scrollbar out to the card's edge with -mr-6, restoring the gutter with
  pr-6 -- both keyed to the card's own px-6), so the title and the nav
  beside it stay put while it moves. The
  options panel is a fixed-height card and wants that; the browser-mode page
  is an ordinary scrolling page and does not, hence the flag rather than a
  hardcoded class. Mirrors AppSettingsSections' prop of the same name.
  The nav beside it scrolls on the same flag and by the same rule, so a
  machine with twenty entries does not run them off the bottom of the card.
#}
{%- set _groups = [
  ("general", "info", "General"),
  ("account", "user", "Account"),
  ("backup", "cloud", "Backup"),
] -%}
{# The machine's name rides in the title, after a separator dot: the panel can
   be opened from the workspace list, where the titlebar crumb does not name it
   either, so otherwise Remove machine sits under a title that could mean any
   of them. The name is capped and truncates -- a long one must not push the
   title into a second line or crowd the close button. #}
<h1 class="type-heading text-primary flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0 shrink-0">
  <Icon16 name="settings" size="lg" extra="shrink-0" />
  <span class="shrink-0">Machine settings:</span>
  <span class="truncate max-w-[280px]">{{ ws_name }}</span>
</h1>

<div id="workspace-settings" data-agent-id="{{ agent_id }}" data-is-stale="{{ 'true' if is_stale else 'false' }}"
     class="mt-8 flex gap-8 flex-1 min-h-0">
  <nav class="shrink-0 w-52 {{ 'overflow-y-auto min-h-0 p-1.5 -m-1.5' if panel_scroll else '' }}" aria-label="Settings groups">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5">
      {% for group_id, icon_name, label in _groups %}
      {% set _selected = group_id == selected_group %}
      <button type="button"
              data-settings-group="{{ group_id }}"
              aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if _selected else 'false' }}"
              class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-left type-body cursor-pointer transition-colors text-primary hover:bg-fill-hover{{ ' bg-fill-hover font-semibold' if _selected else '' }}">
        <Icon16 :name="icon_name" extra="shrink-0" />
        <span class="truncate">{{ label }}</span>
      </button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 {{ 'overflow-y-auto min-h-0 pt-1.5 pb-1.5 pl-1.5 pr-6 -mt-1.5 -mb-1.5 -ml-1.5 -mr-6' if panel_scroll else '' }}">
    <div data-settings-pane="general" class="{{ '' if selected_group == 'general' else 'hidden' }}">
      <SectionHeader>Name</SectionHeader>
      <div id="rename-section" class="mb-8">
        {% if is_stale %}
          <Notice variant="warn">
            This machine is currently unreachable, so it can't be renamed right now.
            Try again once the machine reconnects.
          </Notice>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          {# The design system's input, not a bespoke pill: this one had its own
             surface and radius and no focus ring at all, so it neither matched
             the other fields nor showed keyboard focus. #}
          <TextInput id="workspace-name-input" name="workspace_name" :value="ws_name"
                     maxlength="200" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                     aria-label="Machine name" extra="max-w-xs" :disabled="is_stale" />
          <Button variant="secondary" id="rename-save-btn" :disabled="is_stale">Save</Button>
          <span id="rename-saving-badge" class="hidden type-section text-secondary">Saving...</span>
        </div>
        <p id="rename-error" class="hidden type-body text-important mt-2" role="alert"></p>
      </div>

      {# ``extra`` turns the h2 into a flex row so the badge centers on
         the title's vertical axis; ``leading-none`` + fixed badge height
         keeps the line box from growing when the badge un-hides (which
         would push the swatches down a couple px). #}
      <SectionHeader extra="flex items-center gap-2">Color <span id="color-saving-badge" class="hidden type-section text-primary bg-surface-primary rounded-sm px-1.5 py-1">Saving</span></SectionHeader>
      <div id="color-section" class="mb-8">
        {% if is_stale %}
          <Notice variant="warn">
            This machine is currently unreachable, so its color can't be changed right now.
            Try again once the machine reconnects.
          </Notice>
        {% endif %}
        <div role="radiogroup"
             aria-label="Machine color palette"
             class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3"
             id="color-swatches">
          {% for name, hex_value in palette.items() %}
            <ColorSwatch :hex="hex_value" :name="name" size="md"
                         :selected="hex_value == current_color" :disabled="is_stale" />
          {% endfor %}
          <input id="color-hex-input"
                 type="text"
                 class="color-hex-pill h-[34px] px-3 rounded-full type-body font-mono text-primary placeholder:text-tertiary disabled:opacity-40{{ ' is-selected' if current_color not in palette.values() else '' }}"
                 value="{{ current_color }}"
                 placeholder="#a1b2c3"
                 maxlength="9"
                 spellcheck="false"
                 autocomplete="off"
                 aria-label="Machine color hex"
                 size="8"
                 {% if is_stale %}disabled{% endif %}>
        </div>
        <p id="color-error" class="hidden type-body text-important mt-2" role="alert"></p>
      </div>

      {# The machine's stable identifier, for reading logs or filing a report.
         Read-only on purpose: unlike the name and its host slug (which the
         rename above rewrites together), this never changes. #}
      <SectionHeader>ID</SectionHeader>
      <p class="type-body font-mono text-secondary mb-8 select-all break-all">{{ agent_id }}</p>

      <SectionHeader>Danger zone</SectionHeader>
      <p class="type-body text-secondary mb-3">Permanently destroy this machine and release any associated resources.</p>
      <Button variant="danger" id="destroy-btn">Remove machine</Button>
      <p id="destroy-error" class="hidden type-body text-important mt-2"></p>
    </div>

    <div data-settings-pane="account" class="{{ '' if selected_group == 'account' else 'hidden' }}">
      <SectionHeader>Account</SectionHeader>
      <div id="account-section">
      {% if is_leased_imbue_cloud %}
        {% if current_account %}
          <p class="type-body text-primary mb-3">Linked to <strong>{{ current_account.email }}</strong>.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <Notice variant="info">
          This machine runs on a host leased from Imbue Cloud, so its account
          account link is fixed and cannot be changed.
        </Notice>
        <Button variant="danger" id="disassociate-btn" disabled>Unlink</Button>
      {% elif current_account %}
        <p class="type-body text-primary mb-3">Linked to <strong>{{ current_account.email }}</strong>.</p>
        <Notice variant="warn">
          Unlinking will remove all sharing (tunnels) for this machine.
          You will need to set up sharing again after linking it back.
        </Notice>
        {# The wait is reported inside the button (workspace_settings.js swaps
           its label for "Unlinking..." and a spinner), so there is no
           status text parked beside it. #}
        <Button variant="danger" id="disassociate-btn">Unlink</Button>
        <p id="disassociate-error" class="hidden type-body text-important mt-2" role="alert"></p>
      {% else %}
        <Associate :agent_id="agent_id" :accounts="accounts" />
      {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div data-settings-pane="backup" class="{{ '' if selected_group == 'backup' else 'hidden' }}">
      {# Everything below is main's backups section verbatim, including this
         header's wording -- the nav entry above is a grouping, not a rewrite of
         what backups say or do. (The one omission is SectionHeader's ``divider``:
         it separated sections on a single scrolling page, and inside a pane of
         its own it would draw a rule under nothing.) #}
      <SectionHeader>Backups</SectionHeader>
      <div id="backup-section">
        <p id="backup-status-line" class="type-body text-secondary mb-1"><Spinner size="sm" extra="mr-1" /> Loading backup status...</p>
        <p class="type-helper text-tertiary mb-4">If this machine is destroyed, its backups are kept for 30 days and can be downloaded from the Recently destroyed machines page, then deleted automatically.</p>

        {# Recent backups: workspace_backups.js fills #backup-history from
           /backups (newest-first). "View all" appears when there are more
           than five and opens the full-history page. #}
        <h3 class="type-label text-secondary mb-2">Recent backups</h3>
        <p id="backup-history-empty" class="hidden type-body text-secondary mb-4"></p>
        <div id="backup-history-card" class="minds-card hidden overflow-hidden mb-6 p-0">
          <div id="backup-history"></div>
          <a id="backup-view-all" href={{ "/workspace/" ~ agent_id ~ "/backups" }} style="display: none"
             class="flex items-center gap-1 px-4 py-3 border-t border-default type-body font-semibold text-primary no-underline hover:bg-fill-subtle cursor-pointer">
            <span id="backup-view-all-label">View all backups</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        {# Shared operation strip: one tracked operation (restore, update, or
           storage change) runs per workspace at a time, so its controls live
           here next to the table. Conditional buttons use wrapper spans
           because a `hidden` class loses to the Button's inline-flex display. #}
        <BackupOperationStrip />

        <div id="backup-configure" class="mb-6">
          <h3 class="type-label text-secondary mb-2">Where your backups are stored</h3>
          <p class="type-body text-secondary mb-2 max-w-[560px]">
            Backups are encrypted on your computer, so only you can read them.
            Store them with Imbue or use your own cloud storage.
          </p>
          <Button variant="secondary" id="backup-configure-toggle-btn">Change storage location</Button>
          <div id="backup-configure-form" class="hidden mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <FormLabel target="backup-provider-select">Keep my backups in</FormLabel>
              <select id="backup-provider-select" class="h-[34px] px-3 rounded-full type-body bg-surface-secondary text-primary">
                <option value="IMBUE_CLOUD" {% if not has_account %}disabled{% endif %}>Imbue Cloud (recommended){% if not has_account %} -- requires an account{% endif %}</option>
                <option value="API_KEY" {% if not has_account %}selected{% endif %}>My own cloud storage (advanced)</option>
                <option value="NONE">Nowhere -- turn backups off</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div id="backup-api-key-row" class="hidden">
              <FormLabel target="backup-api-key-env-input">Connection details for your storage</FormLabel>
              <p class="type-helper text-tertiary mb-1 max-w-[560px]">
                Paste the restic environment variables for your storage, one KEY=VALUE per line.
                Leave out RESTIC_PASSWORD -- minds manages the encryption password for you.
              </p>
              <textarea id="backup-api-key-env-input" rows="4" spellcheck="false"
                        class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-md type-body font-mono bg-surface-secondary text-primary"
                        placeholder="RESTIC_REPOSITORY=&#10;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=&#10;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="></textarea>
            </div>
            <div>
              <Button variant="secondary" id="backup-configure-submit-btn">Save</Button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-6">
          <h3 class="type-label text-secondary mb-2">Backup service verification</h3>
          <p class="type-body text-secondary mb-2 max-w-[560px]">
            minds checks your backups regularly and warns you below if anything
            needs attention.
          </p>
          {# The service check execs into the workspace and takes a while;
             workspace_backups.js hides this once the verdict arrives. #}
          <p id="backup-check-loading" class="type-body text-secondary mb-2"><Spinner size="sm" extra="mr-1" /> Checking the backup service...</p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span id="backup-verification-btn-wrap" class="hidden">
              <Button variant="secondary" id="backup-verification-btn">Disable</Button>
            </span>
            <span id="backup-verification-spinner" class="hidden type-section text-secondary"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h3 class="type-label text-secondary mb-2">Fix backup problems</h3>
          <p class="type-body text-secondary mb-2 max-w-[560px]">
            If backups stop working, this reinstalls and restarts the backup software.
            It's safe to run any time and never touches your files or existing backups.
          </p>
          <div id="backup-versions" class="hidden type-helper text-tertiary mb-2"></div>
          <ul id="backup-problems" class="hidden type-body text-important mb-2 list-disc pl-4"></ul>
          <span id="backup-update-btn-wrap" class="hidden">
            <Button variant="secondary" id="backup-update-btn">Update backup software</Button>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<Modal id="destroy-dialog">
  <h2 class="type-heading text-primary mb-3">Remove machine?</h2>
  <p class="type-body text-primary mb-4">This will permanently destroy <strong>{{ ws_name }}</strong> and all its data. This action cannot be undone. Backups are kept for 30 days after destruction, then deleted.</p>
  <div class="flex justify-end gap-3">
    <Button variant="secondary" id="destroy-cancel-btn">Cancel</Button>
    <Button variant="danger" id="destroy-confirm-btn">Remove</Button>
  </div>
</Modal>

{# Unlink confirmation. Unlinking tears down every tunnel for this machine,
   which is not obvious from a button labelled "Unlink" and cannot be undone by
   pressing it again -- sharing has to be set up from scratch afterwards. Same
   shape as the destroy confirmation below it. #}
<Modal id="unlink-dialog">
  <h2 class="type-heading text-primary mb-3">Unlink this machine?</h2>
  <p class="type-body text-primary mb-4">This removes all sharing (tunnels) for <strong>{{ ws_name }}</strong>. You will need to set up sharing again after linking it back.</p>
  <div class="flex justify-end gap-3">
    <Button variant="secondary" id="unlink-cancel-btn">Cancel</Button>
    <Button variant="danger" id="unlink-confirm-btn">Unlink</Button>
  </div>
</Modal>

{# Restore confirmation, opened by a Restore link in the Recent backups table. #}
<RestoreDialog />
